message: "If you use SoPhyFit-Evap, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SoPhyFit-Evap: Soil physics fitting tool for evaporation-method retention and conductivity data"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "Zarebanadkouki"
    given-names: "Mohsen"
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tum-Soil-Biophysics/SoPhyFit-Evap"
url: "https://www.lss.ls.tum.de/sbe/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23628363"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
keywords:
  - HYPROP
  - evaporation method
  - soil water retention curve
  - unsaturated hydraulic conductivity
  - van Genuchten
  - PDI model
  - field capacity
  - confidence intervals
abstract: >-
  SoPhyFit-Evap fits soil water retention and unsaturated hydraulic
  conductivity curves to HYPROP evaporation-method data with six models
  (van Genuchten-Mualem, Brooks-Corey, Kosugi, bimodal van Genuchten, and the
  PDI variants with film flow), using a simultaneous error-weighted fit. It
  reports all parameters, field capacity, wilting point, plant-available water,
  pore classes and the fitted curves with 95% confidence intervals.
